          "result": {
            "message_ref": "msg_asst_8708c004e9b2",
            "answer_excerpt": "The request provides a place name (\"Los Angeles\") without explicit coordinates. I need to call `geo_geocode` to resolve it to a grounded center coordinate and bounding box from OpenStreetMap Nominatim. Since no explicit radius was stated, I'll use a conservative regional analysis radius (e.g., 75 km for a metropolitan area) and document that assumption in warnings. The provenance will be `osm_nominatim`.\n\nThe geo_geocode tool successfully returned Los Angeles coordinates from OpenStreetMap Nominatim:\n- Center: lat 34.0536909, lon -118.242766\n- Bbox: [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306]\n- High confidence (importance 0.84, administrative-level entity)\n\nSince no explicit radius was provided in the request, I'll set a conservative regional-analysis radius of 75 km for the Los Angeles metropolitan area. This covers the urban core and surrounding suburbs where GNSS stations are typically deployed. I'll document this as an assumed default in warnings.\n\nNow I'll submit the resolved geospatial evidence for downstream data discovery.\n\nLos Angeles resolved to center 34.0537°N, 118.2428°W (Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California) with a regional-analysis radius of 75 km covering the metropolitan area.",
